  "contracts": [
    "Capture a private retained Arc identity for current credential cache before external source selection and any load await.",
    "Compare captured revision against current revision under credential write lock before equality comparisons, replacement/None clearing or permanent failure publication; mismatch is private CredentialsChanged.",
    "Prepare a new revision only for a real auths_equal_for_refresh transition, before policy lock; swap credentials, failure and revision with exact current policy; drop retired values after locks.",
    "No-op credential replacement and failure-only updates preserve revision; real token replacement, logout clearing and A-to-B-to-A transitions invalidate older candidates.",
    "Public reload remains bool and guarded reload retains Skipped/ReloadedChanged/ReloadedNoChange; no public revision API, serde representation, dependency or persisted schema change."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Candidate is a connected native cache-publication prerequisite, not independently installed catalog/auth extraction or broker activation.",
    "Credential revision is not external-source registry identity. Equal-byte source swap, pending install/clear arbitration and outer external refresh failure publication remain separate follow-up work.",
    "Provider-owned internal token mutation, shared/persistent auth writes, durable logout and restart provenance are not fenced here.",
    "Returned credentials are point-in-time acquisitions, not future dispatch permits; initial command self-acquisition, explicit-key routing, gateway retained work, every retry, response lifetime and conditional model-cache publication remain outside this slice.",
    "Actual HTTP tests use an intentionally account-unbound existing loopback factory. They do not prove account-bound factory revival/revocation; a revoked caller factory must not be silently replaced.",
    "No fresh full-CLI/GUI/storage runtime proof follows from package tests. The published 192d353 full-host checkpoint predates this proposal and remains separate.",
    "Pinned upstream revision and component/package contracts are unchanged. No updater/migration/rollback acceptance or P00M checker support/current-index closure is asserted; historical lineage/index/evidence remain immutable."
  ],
